Position Summary

The Physical Security Engineer provides regional engineering leadership for physical security systems throughout the planning, design, construction, and commissioning lifecycle. This role ensures every new data center is designed and deployed in accordance with Nscale's global physical security standards while serving as the primary regional engineering authority.

The Physical Security Engineer works closely with architects, consultants, system integrators, and the Data Center Infrastructure organization to ensure physical security requirements are incorporated early into project designs and maintained through final delivery.

Primary Responsibilities

• Review architectural and engineering designs for compliance with Nscale standards.&nbsp;

• Partner with DCI during planning and design development.&nbsp;

• Review security consultant designs, shop drawings, and equipment submittals.&nbsp;

• Evaluate proposed changes to scope and specifications.&nbsp;

• Serve as technical approval authority for physical security design changes.&nbsp;

• Support engineering coordination throughout construction.&nbsp;

• Perform installation quality inspections and milestone walkthroughs.&nbsp;

• Support commissioning and operational turnover activities.&nbsp;

• Provide technical support during construction and issue resolution.&nbsp;

• Serve as the regional technical subject matter expert for physical security design and systems engineering.&nbsp;

Success Measures

• Reduced design changes during construction.
